subnapi (0.5.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ignore subtitle credit lines that do not name an author when uploading
    to NapiProjekt: download stamps left by subtitle sites ("Napisy pobrane
    z ...:"), song credits ("Tekst piosenki:") and "przekład" credits. Such
    lines were previously uploaded as the subtitle author.

 -- mskpluk <mskpluk@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0000

subnapi (0.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Detect subtitle authors from more credit lines when uploading to
    NapiProjekt: recognise "Napisy:", widen the searched tail of the file,
    and rank the labels so a translator credit wins over a broadcaster or
    studio credit. Files crediting "Napisy: ..." were previously uploaded
    with an empty author.

 -- mskpluk <mskpluk@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0000

subnapi (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First Subnapi release. Subnapi is a Linux-only fork of QNapi
    (https://github.com/QNapi/qnapi, inactive upstream since 2022).
  * Restore NapiProjekt subtitle upload and correction support (removed
    from QNapi in 0.2.2 when the old API died), reimplemented against
    the current NapiProjekt API: GUI upload/correction dialog, a
    directory scan-and-review batch flow, and -u/--upload, -r/--correct
    switches in the command-line client.
  * Add a napiprojekt: URI scheme handler with xdg-mime registration.
  * Add desktop notifications (DBus, with tray fallback).
  * Port the application from Qt5 to Qt6.
  * Fix UTF-16 LE subtitle processing.
  * Drop Windows/macOS support, packaging and bundled prebuilt
    binaries; Linux-only.
  * ~/.config/qnapi.ini is copied to ~/.config/subnapi.ini
    on first run under the new name; the original file is untouched.

 -- mskpluk <mskpluk@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
